<title>UK: Rolls-Royce wins 10 mln stg award from BNFL.</title>
<headline>Rolls-Royce wins 10 mln stg award from BNFL.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rolls-Royce Plc said on Thursday that its unit has won a contract worth more than 10 million stg from BNFL Engineering Ltd, the engineering arm of British Nuclear Fuels (BNFL).</p>
<p>The contract calls for Rolls-Royce Nuclear Engineering Services to to design and supply two silo emptying machines. The building programme is phased over the next four years, with the first machine scheduled to leave the factory in 1999.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
